Between Karen's desk and the printer stands someone who did not
walk there. Water runs off him steadily, from his hair, his
sleeves, the hem of a coat that has been under the mere a long
time. He looks at Osei, only at Osei, across the whole length of
the room, with great patience. One of the Drowned, who come up
out of the mere when the bell rings wrong. The water leaves him
in one thin line along the seams of the carpet, and the line
is coming toward Osei's desk.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2 · render: fallback]
The older guard sees it. He walks toward Osei to cut the line
off. The artificer steps into his way.
The guard lifts his gun and fires.
The sound is enormous and short. The artificer brings the brass
arm up across his face, not quickly, as a man lifts an arm
against rain. The shot strikes it, and the arm rings: one clear
note, deep and bronze, much too big for the arm, the way a bell
sounds under water. It goes out across the floor and comes back
off the long window. Twelve people go on typing. The guard takes
a step back as if the note has pushed him, and the artificer
swings the arm round in a long low arc, and the guard goes
sideways into a filing cabinet, slides down it, and gets up at
once with exactly the same expression.
The water reaches the leg of Osei's desk and pools there.

