head comes on blue. Then one by the window. Then one in
Haldane's glass office, where nobody has turned on a lamp in a
week. Then one at the lift lobby. Four blue lamps, each at the
end of its own thin line of water.
The partner looks at the four lamps. He goes to Haldane's office
first. The lamp inside goes out as his hand touches the door. He
turns and walks to the lift lobby. That lamp goes out as he
reaches it. He doesn't seem annoyed. He looks at his watch, as if
two short delays have been entered against his name, and goes
back to the line of water by the window and follows that one
instead.
